<article class="detail-page"><a class="detail-back" href="/insights/">← Back to insights</a><div class="section-label">Operations & SOPs</div><h1>The 8 KPIs Every MSME Operations Leader Should Track Weekly (and How to Build a Power BI Dashboard for Them)</h1><div class="detail-content modal-body"><p>Most MSMEs track revenue and maybe profit. The businesses that scale sustainably track the operational metrics that predict revenue and profit — before they show up in the P&L.</p><h4>The 8 Essential KPIs</h4><p><strong>1. On-Time-In-Full (OTIF)</strong> — % of orders delivered complete and on time. Target: 95%+. This single metric predicts customer retention better than NPS.<br><strong>2. Inventory Days on Hand</strong> — How many days of sales your current stock covers. Too high = cash trapped. Too low = stockout risk.<br><strong>3. Procurement Cost vs Budget</strong> — Are you buying at the rates you planned? Variance of more than 5% needs explanation.<br><strong>4. Throughput per Employee</strong> — Revenue or units produced per headcount. The best proxy for operational productivity.<br><strong>5. Defect / Error Rate</strong> — % of orders, products, or processes with quality failures. Should trend downward every quarter.<br><strong>6. Vendor On-Time Delivery</strong> — % of supplier deliveries arriving on time. Poor supplier OTD is the most common hidden cause of customer-facing delays.<br><strong>7. Cash Conversion Cycle</strong> — Days inventory + days receivable - days payable. The shorter this is, the less working capital you need to grow.<br><strong>8. SOP Compliance Rate</strong> — % of processes being followed as documented. Businesses with high SOP compliance have 40% fewer operational failures.</p></div><a class="btn-primary" href="/#contact">Request a Discovery Call →</a></article>
</Layout>
